{#
  Marquee ticker.

  `.ticker-clip` is load-bearing: it clips the stripe's overhang so a rotated,
  over-wide element cannot widen the document. Removing it reintroduces horizontal
  page overflow, which is why the live markup carries the same wrapper and why the
  validator checks for it rather than trusting the CSS.

  The phrase run is stored ONCE in the record and repeated `tickerRuns` times here,
  because the CSS translation needs a second copy in place as the first leaves.
  That count is IT machinery (src/_data/homeTechnical.js), not content.

  The whole ticker is aria-hidden, so assistive technology never reaches either
  copy — the repetition raises no accessibility question on this page.

  Expects: home, locale, homeTechnical
#}
<div class="ticker-clip">
  <div class="ticker" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="ticker-track">
{%- for run in range(0, homeTechnical.tickerRuns) %}
      <span>{% for phrase in home.ticker.phrases %}{{ phrase[locale.code] }} <span class="dot"></span> {% endfor %}</span>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
